{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "תאומים", :translit "te'omim", :gloss "twins"} {:he "חסר יו\"ד וא'", :translit "chaser yud v'alef", :gloss "defective (of) yod and alef"} {:he "י\"א", :translit "echad asar", :gloss "eleven"} {:he "י\"א שבטים", :translit "echad asar shvatim", :gloss "eleven tribes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "א'", :b "י\"א"}], :frame {:text "The word תאומים in Genesis 25:24 is written defectively as תומם. Ba'al HaTurim takes the missing letter alef (gematria 1) as hinting to the number eleven — the total of tribes Rebecca was destined to bear. She bore Esau and Jacob, from whom came the twelve tribes, but since Esau did not produce a tribe of Israel, Rebecca effectively mothered eleven tribes (Genesis 35:23–26 enumerates Jacob's twelve sons; the扣除 of Esau leaves eleven).", :sources ["Genesis 25:24" "Genesis 35:23-26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "א'", :a-value 1, :b "י\"א", :b-value 11, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:57.312499056Z", :model "glm-5.2"}